Z||000000||RobH||05-15-2000||10:49 PM||||Can this be put into a Fiero?  Someone pointed this out to me today and said this would be an awesome little engine...comes pretty much fully assembled.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.gmgoodwrench.com/crate_engine/global/ix_ht34.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmgoodwrench.com/crate_engine/global/ix_ht34.htm</A> <P>Isn't the motor in a Fiero actually for a front-wheel drive vehicle?  If so, I don't think this would work, but who knows...||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-15-2000||10:55 PM||||I'm not sure of the part #, but a 3.4L crate engine is available from Ed Parks or Bob Steiger and probably others who do engine switches.  Thos are about the stats that is given for the 3.4L that is put into a Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||05-16-2000||04:03 AM||||You would have to drill starter holes on the other side of the block, but that's it.  the 160hp is with a small carb and stock s-10 exhaust, i think.  It should a bit higher with fuel injection and ported fiero manifolds.  the part number is 12363230||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||05-16-2000||05:05 AM||||Im looking to replace my killer 4 banger with :  <A HREF="http://www.gmgoodwrench.com/crate_engine/global/ix_zz.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gmgoodwrench.com/crate_engine/global/ix_zz.htm</A> <P>I was going to go with a charged V6, but what the he//.. everyone I talked to told me to just go with a V8.  <P><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 05-16-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000004||Alex4mula||05-16-2000||09:29 AM||||That's a GM 3.4 and not 2.8. Yes it will fit perfectly in the Fiero. Major mod is the starter holes but depending on year some other parts/bracket matching has to be done. I am currently installing one in my Formula. Got it ready from Ed Parks (Fiero Factory).||||reg||1
Z||000005||87PegasusGT||05-16-2000||01:24 PM||||Yup. In fact I just got mine done. Talk about fun. A fiero owner can tell its not stock because it does look bigger, but anyone else couldn't tell.||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||05-16-2000||03:05 PM||||The overall dimensions are identical to the 2.8. The big diff between the blocks is the reenforcements on the sides. 2.8s are smooth. Contrary to what they say, 3.4s are alive and well and in California! The smog man never knows.....||||reg||6
Z||000007||Alex4mula||05-16-2000||03:43 PM||||I have both in front of me currently working on my swap and they look identical in size. Some ribs here and studs there are different but hard to see at galnce view. The 3.4 is more beautiful!:-)||||reg||7
